Z||000003||fierojunky||01-31-2001||10:04 AM||||i just put that same set up in my car!  your going to have one slot that dosn't get a plug.  These radios were used with a remote cassette player so the one plug is for that.  Also be sure you get the antenna adapter.  As for the wiring to make it simpler i went to a local stero shop and got a wiring harness adapter for both ends so its just plug and play.  Sounds great too!!||||reg||14
Z||000004||TheFiero64||01-31-2001||11:21 AM||||Hope you enjoy it. I thought I used all the plugs.<P>I thought the up3 was this one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mar14%5e02.jpg">  <P>Is there 2 Gen. of UP3's? <p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
