Z||000007||tgowens||01-31-2001||12:26 PM||||Fiero64, that is an older Delco version of the UP3, the other UP3 comes specifically from the Pontiac and is found in the later years (generally from '95 on to 2000 models...) The newer UP3 does not use the third plug - just the long black plug and the smaller blue plug.<P>Fierojunky is correct, there is a third receptacle in the middle of the back of the radio for a remote CD changer however, that uses a separate wiring lead........<P>As I mentioned before, the extra plugs on the wiring adapter are not used in a Pontiac application.........<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">    </A>||||reg||1
